# Line endings.
#
# This repository ships shell scripts that bash executes inside Termux, on
# Android. A CRLF script fails there immediately and confusingly: bash reads the
# carriage return as part of the last token on every line, so the run dies with
# `$'\r': command not found`, `syntax error near unexpected token $'{\r'` and
# `umask: 077: octal number out of range` from the first few lines.
#
# The blobs here are LF and need to stay LF. Without this file a Windows
# checkout converts them on the way out, each one then shows up as a whole-file
# diff, and committing from that checkout publishes scripts that cannot run on
# the device the plugin targets. That conversion is also why LICENSE has been
# permanently "modified".
#
# `text=auto eol=lf`: decide text vs binary by content, check text out with LF
# on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Stated again for the files where the wrong ending is fatal rather than
# cosmetic: the three Termux scripts and the suite that runs them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# CI compares build output byte for byte; leave these alone.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jar binary
